.TH SOCTRIAGE 1 "2026-04-21" "soctriage 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soctriage \- AI-powered Linux kernel / SoC crash diagnostic tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soctriage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I LOG_FILE
.br
.B soctriage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-\-input
.I PATH
.br
.B soctriage
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soctriage
analyses Linux kernel crash logs and SoC diagnostic dumps to identify the root
cause of hardware failures, classify subsystem events, and generate structured
reports. An optional Anthropic Claude or Ollama LLM backend produces human-readable
root-cause narratives and fix suggestions.
.PP
The pipeline: open_log \(-> tokenize \(-> assemble \(-> classify \(-> hardware_decode
\(-> cascade_analyse \(-> run_agent \(-> report.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input / Output
.TP
.B LOG_FILE
Kernel log file (.log, .gz, .bz2, .xz) or \fB\-\fR for stdin.
.TP
.BI \-\-input " PATH"
Input log file path, or \fB\-\fR for stdin (alias for positional argument).
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Output report base path. Extension added per \fB\-\-format\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " {json,markdown,html}"
Output format (default: json).
.TP
.B \-\-include\-raw
Include raw event text in JSON output.
.SS LLM Control
.TP
.B \-\-no\-llm
Skip LLM agent. Run Phase 4 cascade analysis only.
.TP
.BI \-\-llm\-backend " {anthropic,ollama}"
LLM backend (default: anthropic).
.TP
.BI \-\-llm\-model " MODEL"
LLM model name (default: claude-sonnet-4-5).
.TP
.BI \-\-ollama\-host " URL"
Ollama API host (default: http://localhost:11434).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
LLM call timeout in seconds (default: 60).
.SS SoC / Hardware
.TP
.BI \-\-asic\-gen " GEN"
Override ASIC/chip generation detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-soc\-provider " NAME"
Force specific SoC provider by name.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-providers
List all registered providers and exit.
.SS Extensibility
.TP
.BI \-\-token\-rule " TYPE:PATTERN"
Inject an inline token rule. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-plugin " PATH"
Load a Python plugin file containing @register_rule rules. Repeatable.
.SS Utility
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show soctriage version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \(em no critical events, or log was clean.
.TP
.B 1
Critical severity event detected in the log.
.TP
.B 2
Runtime error (file not found, parse failure, agent failure).
.TP
.B 3
Usage error (bad arguments).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Analyse a kernel log without LLM:
.B soctriage /var/log/dmesg \-\-no\-llm
.TP
Save HTML report:
.B soctriage crash.log \-\-no\-llm \-\-format html \-\-output report.html
.TP
Full analysis with Anthropic Claude:
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-... soctriage crash.log
.TP
Force AMD provider:
.B soctriage crash.log \-\-soc\-provider amd \-\-no\-llm
.TP
Read from stdin:
.B dmesg | soctriage \- \-\-no\-llm
.TP
Analyse compressed log:
.B soctriage crash.log.gz \-\-no\-llm
.TP
Inject an inline token rule:
.B soctriage crash.log \-\-token\-rule "cxl_event:CXL 3.0: fatal" \-\-no\-llm
.TP
Use Ollama locally:
.B soctriage crash.log \-\-llm\-backend ollama \-\-llm\-model llama3.2
.TP
Save JSON with raw event text:
.B soctriage crash.log \-\-no\-llm \-\-include\-raw \-\-output report.json
.TP
List available SoC providers:
.B soctriage \-\-list\-providers
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Required for \fB\-\-llm\-backend anthropic\fR.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Override Ollama API host without using \fB\-\-ollama\-host\fR.
.TP
.B SOCTRIAGE_RULES_DIR
Override the bundled YAML token rules directory.
.TP
.B SOCTRIAGE_LOG_LEVEL
Python logging level for soctriage internals (default: WARNING).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colour in terminal output when set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/soctriage/custom.yaml
Optional user-level custom token rules (loaded automatically if present).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmesg (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR python3 (1)
